-- title:
--   Level-one q-expansions at q² lie in the λ-field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Work inside the field `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` of formal Laurent series. Write `fieldOver (1 * q) K` for the subfield generated by the constant series coming from the ring of integers-free subring underlying $K$ (the image of $K$ under `CharPReduction.constSeries`, i.e. the composite of the inclusion of $K$ with the structure map into Laurent series) together with the two elements `jqModC`, the series $\mathfrak q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum` with coefficients pushed into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and `jqNModC (1 * q)`, its image under the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{1\cdot q}$. Write `lambdaFieldOver q K` for the subfield generated by the same constants together with `lambdaModC`, the coefficientwise image of the integral series `lambdaInt`, and `lambdaNModC q`, its image under $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$. The assertion is: for every $x \in$ `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the series obtained from $x$ by the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{2}$, namely `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) 2 x`, lies in `lambdaFieldOver q K`.
--
--   This records, at the level of $q$-expansions, the classical fact that the $j$-invariant is a rational function of the Legendre $\lambda$-function (here in the normalisation $\mu = \lambda/16$), so that the level-one function field read after the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{2}$ sits inside the field generated by $\lambda(\mathfrak q)$ and $\lambda(\mathfrak q^{q})$. It is used in the analysis of the node localisation on the $\lambda$-model, for instance in the integrality and localisation statements for `lambdaFieldOver` and in the identification of the completed local ring at a point with $j$-invariant $0$ or $1728$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized_qExpand_two_mem_lambdaFieldOver_of_mem_fieldOver.lean

